            <ArticleTitle>Churg-Strauss syndrome: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/0100-3984.2013.1817</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss syndrome is a rare systemic disease primarily characterized by hypereosinophilia, asthma and vasculitis. The lung is the organ most frequently involved. In the present report, the authors describe a relatively rare finding in this disease - the presence of a pulmonary nodule -, while recalling the main radiological findings and the most relevant differential diagnoses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
